**Definition 3.2 (singular atoms).** Define

$$
\mathcal C_2=\left\{\sum_{j=1}^m z_jz_j^\dagger:
 m<\infty,\quad (z_j)_0\bigl((z_j)_0^2-\alpha(z_j)_1^2-
 \beta(z_j)_2^2\bigr)=0\right\}.
\tag{CA.16}
$$

The empty sum is zero. Here an atom means a rank-one **coefficient
projector** in this generating cone. It is not a claim of canonical
factor irreducibility, a unique decomposition or universal ontology.
Let $J:\mathbb C^2\to\mathbb C^3$ include the last two coefficient
coordinates. The plane atoms sum to matrices $JWJ^\dagger$, $W\succeq0$.

